# Architecture boundaries

## Dependency rule

- Domain → SharedKernel + BCL only.
- Application → Domain + SharedKernel; owns use cases + ports.
- Infrastructure → Application/Domain/Contracts; implements ports.
- Api = composition root; no business policy.
- Contracts = external HTTP/event schemas only.
- Migrations = independent deployable; never from API startup.
- Production code never references test projects.

## Modules

Identity, Knowledge, Research, Content, Catalog, Publication, Commerce, Learning.

- Mutate only own aggregates/tables.
- Cross-module writes via application command or integration event.
- Cross-module reads via explicit query ports + purpose DTOs.
- No shared entities across modules; cycles fail architecture tests.

## Forbidden

`IRepository<T>`, custom UoW, BaseService/CrudService/Manager/Utils dumps, provider SDKs in Domain/Application, status field assignment outside aggregate/policy.

## GoF

Strategy/Adapter/Factory/Builder/Observer/Decorator/CoR/Facade — only with named variation. Prefer Wolverine/.NET pipelines over reinvented mediators.
